index 3bcff7077..1a658a9fe 100644
--- a/apps/swarmagents/README.md
+++ b/apps/swarmagents/README.md
@@ -187,14 +187,39 @@ Every tool call the agent makes passes through the pure risk classifier in
 | `ask` | Risky but legitimate; pauses for a human decision. | `rm -rf /` or other destructive root deletions, `curl \| sh` / piping a remote download into a shell, downloads from untrusted hosts, `docker`/`podman` and other container commands, force/destructive git operations, reading or writing credential files (`~/.ssh`, `.env`, `.aws`, ...), privilege elevation (`sudo`), disk/partition tools, broad `chmod`/`chown`, system package-manager mutations, service control, firewall changes, `ssh`/`scp`/`rsync` |
 | `deny` | Never allowed; no approval can lift it. | printing secret environment variables, system credential files (`/etc/passwd`, `/etc/shadow`, `/etc/sudoers`, ...), referencing secret env vars with a disclosure verb, cloud instance metadata endpoints (`169.254.169.254` and equivalents) |
 
-An `ask`-level decision pauses the run: the runner creates a pending approval
-in the in-memory `ApprovalStore` (`lib/harness/approvals.ts`) and the user
-decides with `POST /api/runtime/approvals/{id}` (approve or deny) from the
-terminal's approval card. If nobody decides before the TTL expires the
-approval auto-expires and is treated exactly like a denial — the run halts
-with a `run.error` under the harness risk policy. The pending store is
-per-process: a server restart drops pending approvals (their runs end with a
-policy error rather than hanging forever).
+The verdict is **synchronous with execution**: the VM's Claude Code settings
+register a `PreToolUse` hook (`vm-image/pretooluse-hook.mjs`), so the CLI runs
+that hook before every tool and blocks until it answers. The hook calls
+`POST /api/runtime/hooks/pretooluse` with the per-run bearer token; the app
+classifies the call and replies with the Claude Code permission decision
+(`lib/harness/tool-gate.ts`). A tool therefore executes only after it was
+allowed — a denial, or a timeout, means the command never ran at all.
+
+An `ask`-level decision creates a pending approval in the in-memory
+`ApprovalStore` (`lib/harness/approvals.ts`) while the CLI is blocked on the
+hook; the user decides with `POST /api/runtime/approvals/{id}` (approve or
+deny) from the terminal's approval card. If nobody decides before the TTL
+expires the approval auto-expires and the hook answers `deny` — the model sees
+the reason and can adapt, and nothing ran. The pending store is per-process: a
+server restart drops pending approvals (their runs end with a policy error
+rather than hanging forever).
+
+- The hook fails closed: an unreachable app, a bad token, a malformed payload
+  or an unreadable verdict all answer `deny`.
+- The gate token is minted per run, lives in memory, is revoked when the run
+  ends, and can only *ask* — holding it cannot approve anything.
+- A duplicate hook (the image's managed settings plus a run `--settings`
+  file) is deduped by tool-call id: one card, one decision.
+- VMs built from an image that predates the hook get it through a per-run
+  `--settings` file (`lib/runtime/hook-settings.ts`); if the hook never calls
+  home at all, the runner keeps the older stdout-based gate as a fallback.
+- `SWARM_VM_HOOK_BASE_URL` sets the app origin the VM calls back on; it
+  defaults to the LLM proxy origin (`SWARM_VM_LLM_BASE_URL`, else
+  `SWARM_PUBLIC_ORIGIN` in server mode). Without a reachable origin the
+  synchronous gate is not wired and the fallback gate applies.
+- `SWARM_FULL_AUTO=1` (g9 full-auto) auto-allows the asks that stay inside the
+  VM. Hard denies and irreversible-external actions (force push, publish,
+  deploy, cloud API mutations) still open a card.
 
 - TTL: `SWARM_APPROVAL_TIMEOUT_SEC` (seconds, default `300`).
   `SWARM_APPROVAL_TIMEOUT_MS` remains supported as a fallback for
@@ -334,6 +359,8 @@ Never commit real keys. All provider keys live in env only.
 | `SWARM_VM_ENV_ALLOW` | unset | Comma-separated extra env var names forwarded into VMs. |
 | `CLAUDE_BIN` | `claude` | Path to the Claude Code CLI binary inside the VM. |
 | `SWARM_APPROVAL_TIMEOUT_SEC` | `300` | Seconds before an unanswered ask-level approval auto-denies and halts the run. |
+| `SWARM_VM_HOOK_BASE_URL` | unset | App origin a VM calls back on for the `PreToolUse` approval hook (defaults to the LLM proxy origin / `SWARM_PUBLIC_ORIGIN`). Without it the synchronous gate is not wired. |
+| `SWARM_FULL_AUTO` | unset | `1` = g9 full-auto: auto-allow in-VM asks; hard denies and irreversible-external actions still ask. |
 | `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | unset | Provider key forwarded to the VM for Claude Code. |
 | `SWARM_KEYS_ANTHROPIC` / `SWARM_KEYS_OPENAI` / `SWARM_KEYS_GEMINI` | unset | Comma-separated key pools for the provider router. |
 | `SWARM_HEDGE_DELAY_MS` | `1500` | Hedge delay in ms before a second healthy provider starts when hedged racing is enabled and no first token has arrived. |
